# All-player Custom Plan browsing

Add an All option to the Custom Plan selector and identify each visible plan by its owner colour.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The Custom tab selector adds a circular All option divided into slices representing the six player colours.
- [x] Selecting All displays saved custom plans belonging to every player.
- [x] Each custom plan row shows a small ownership dot matching its `PlayerColor` beside the plan name.
- [x] Selecting an individual colour continues to show only that player's plans and statistics.
- [x] The Default tab retains individual-player behavior and does not offer All unless separately specified.
- [x] New Plan remains available in All mode.
- [x] Creating from All opens SCR-004 with Red selected by default.
- [x] The editor offers only the six individual colours; changing colour before Save assigns the plan to that player.
- [x] If the untouched generated default name changes owner, it is recomputed from that owner's same-kind plans; a user-edited name is preserved.
- [x] After Save, the All list shows the plan with the correct ownership dot and individual filtering shows it only for its owner.
- [x] Switching between All and individual colours preserves custom plans and table scroll integrity.
- [x] Domain/filtering and UI regression coverage compile for all six players.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- The All choice is Plan Browser presentation state, not a seventh `PlayerColor`, and must not be serialized as an owner.
- Default naming is calculated from Red when creation begins in All mode and follows the per-owner rules in TASK-022 if the owner changes before the generated name is edited.

## Evidence

- Added a six-slice All control that is presentation-only and leaves `PlayerColor` unchanged.
- Custom rows use owner-aware statistics, display colour ownership dots, and filter through a domain helper covered for all six players.
- New plans created from All start as Red; untouched generated names follow owner changes while edited names remain intact.
- Extended the custom-plan UI regression flow to cover All visibility, ownership, Red-default creation, and editor colour changes.
- `xcodebuild build-for-testing` compiled the app, unit tests, and UI tests using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-tasks025-030-derived`; live simulator execution remains for manual verification.
